WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.752
That's it.

3
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.992
Can I just. you know.
look at it for a minute?

4
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.275
You're an artist. Sid.

5
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.759
You're telling me you're gonna walk
outta here and I'm never gonna see it again?

6
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.593
There's a good chance of that. yes.

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.036
Most guys. for the first one.
they start with something small.

8
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.918
'Mom'. girlfriend's initials.
something like that.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.275
Not you.

10
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.511
You get a full set of sleeves
all in a couple of months.

11
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.831
It takes guys a few years
to get the ink you got.

12
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.195
I don't have a few years.

13
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.395
Wish to hell I did.

14
00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:00.391
- The vault. Open it.
- We can't. The branch manager's not here.

15
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.392
- Where is he?
- It's lunchtime. He's at White Castle.

16
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.516
- White Castle?
- A fast-food restaurant.

17
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.239
They serve those little square burgers.

18
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.311
I know what it is.

19
00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.590
I'm not playing games. Open it.

20
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.266
Sir. you have half a million dollars cash...

21
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:20.312
in your bag. Don't you
think it'd be better if...?

22
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.275
This is the police.
You are completely surrounded.

23
00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.755
Put down your weapon.

24
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.549
Put down your weapons now!

25
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.079
Rarely in the case of armed robbery
do we hear a plea of no contest.

26
00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.232
- Are you sure about this. Mr Scofield?
- I'm sure. Your Honour.

27
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.518
Your Honour. we'd like to recess if we could.
My client's a bit confused.

28
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.636
- I'm not.
- He is. Your Honour.

29
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.794
Perhaps you should heed her advice. Take
additional time to consider your response.

30
00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.952
I've already done that. Your Honour.

31
00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:17.116
I'll retire to my chambers to determine
sentencing. Court's recessed until 1:30.

32
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.595
- Hey. Come on. Let's go.
- Uncle Mike?

33
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.835
I didn't want you to come.
Go home. LJ.

34
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.388
I didn't want you to see this.

35
00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.072
- He won't take this well.
- Can you blame him? He's your nephew.

36
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.438
He's beginning to think anybody he attaches
himself to is gonna end up in prison.

37
00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.559
And he's not the only one
who's starting to feel that way. Michael.

38
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.598
- Will you give us a minute?
- One minute.

39
00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.398
Don't you understand?

40
00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.995
You put the book in that woman's hand.
She'll lob it at you like a grenade.

41
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.435
Justice and punishment
are the same thing to her.

42
00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.669
I know.

43
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.230
- So tell me what's going through your head.
- We've been over this.

44
00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.835
I've known you all my life.
You don't have a violent bone in your body.

45
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.559
- And I know you didn't need the money.
- Veronica...

46
00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:14.351
- Why won't you let me help you?
- You've been good to me my whole life.

47
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.910
But you gotta let me deal with this. OK?

48
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.596
Given your lack of prior criminal conduct.
I am inclined toward probation.

49
00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:28.038
But the fact you discharged a weapon while
committing the crime suggests malice to me.

50
00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:34.070
For that reason. I find it incumbent that you
see the inside of a prison cell. Mr Scofield.

51
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:38.517
You've requested to be incarcerated
near your home here in Chicago.

52
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.192
I'm willing to honour that.

53
00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.432
- The closest level one facility...
- Level one? That's maximum security.

54
00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.717
I would ask counsel
to refrain from interrupting me.

55
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:52.316
As I was saying. the closest level one facility
would be Fox River State Penitentiary.

56
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.312
As for your sentence.
I'm setting it at five years.

57
00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.235
You'll be eligible for parole in half that time.
Sentence to be carried out immediately.

58
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:17.313
OK. people. step inside the door. Check
yourself for bugs. Keep the line moving.

59
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.153
We ain't got all day to get this done.

60
00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.390
No talking in line.

61
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.155
Keep that line moving.
Keep it moving. Next.

62
00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.669
- Name and bank number.
- Scofield. Michael. 94941.

63
00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.228
- You a religious man?
- Never thought about it.

64
00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:39.915
Good. cos the Ten Commandments
don't mean piss in here. We got two only.

65
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.434
The first commandment is.
you got nothin' comin'.

66
00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.876
- What's the second commandment?
- See commandment number one.

67
00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.316
- Gotcha.
- You talking out the side of your neck?

68
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.075
- Come again?
- I said. are you bein' a smartass?

69
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:58.032
Just trying to fly low. avoid the radar. boss.
Do my time and get out.

70
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.788
- There isn't any flyin' under my radar.
- Good to know.

71
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:27.112
Can't a brother get some air conditioning
up here? It's hotter than a crack ho's mouth.

72
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.478
To hell with the AC. man.
Gimme the crack ho.

73
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.195
Come on!

74
00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:42.553
Yo. fish. What you lookin' at?
You look kinda pretty to be up in here. man.

75
00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.198
Fish!

76
00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:50.593
I suggest you take a seat. fish.
Ain't nothing to do up in here but serve time.

77
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.432
Ain't nobody gonna serve it for you.

78
00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.432
Argh!

79
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.794
Welcome to Prisneyland. fish.

80
00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:17.070
- Attention. all prisoners...

81
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.030
- You wanna talk about it?
- It's not worth talking about.

82
00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:42.193
- If it's keeping you up it is.
- No. it's just...

83
00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.919
It's nothing. you know.

84
00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.675
- Michael's case.
- You did the best you could.

85
00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.432
But he didn't.

86
00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:56.355
He just rolled over. he didn't put up a fight.
It's not like him. I...

87
00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:03.799
- I'm sorry. I shouldn't be talking about him.
- Hey. if it's on your mind. it's on your mind.

88
00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.871
Good night.

89
00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:19.399
All lanes. start coming out.
All lanes. start coming out.

90
00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.439
Trey Street Deuces got the hoops.
Norte�os got the bleachers.

91
00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.193
Woods got the weight pile.

92
00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.593
The COs got the rest. I tell you. the guards
have the dirtiest gang in this whole place.

93
00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:38.036
The only difference between us and them
is the badge.

94
00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.998
- Who's the pet lover?
- He'll deny it. but he's DB Cooper.

95
00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.868
Parachuted out of a plane 30 years ago
with a million and a half in cash.

96
00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.428
- Doesn't look like the type.
- Who does?

97
00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.114
Hey! Whaddup. Wholesale? You OK?

98
00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.715
Gonna be greater later.
What you doin' with this fish. man?

99
00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:58.191
He's my new cellie. Wholesale's
got it wired up at the commissary.

100
00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.111
Anything you want. he can get it.

101
00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.794
You keep handin' out my jacket.
I'll bust your grape.

102
00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:09.479
You couldn't bust a grape in Napa with a set
of cleats on. What are you talkin' about?

103
00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.195
I'm looking for someone.

104
00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.317
- Guy named Lincoln Burrows.
- Linc the Sink?

105
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.550
- That what they're calling him now?
- Yeah.

106
00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:47.349
As in. he'll come at you
with everything but the kitchen. snowflake.

107
00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.078
Where can I find him?

108
00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.631
Man killed the VP's brother.
In a month he's getting the chair.

109
00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.793
Which means no one here's more dangerous
than him. cos he's got nothing to lose now.

110
00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.316
- What are they gonna do. kill him twice?
- Any way I can get to him?

111
00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.278
The only time those boys get out
is for chapel and Pl.

112
00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:07.352
- Pl? What's that?
- Prison industry.

113
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:13.390
The guys that get along get to work - painting.
scrubbing. making mattresses. you name it.

114
00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:17.029
I wouldn't get excited if I were you. fish.
You ain't sniffin' none of Pl.

115
00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.669
- Why's that?
- Cos John Abruzzi runs it.

116
00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:24.435
- 'John Abruzzi' John Abruzzi?
- 'John Abruzzi' John Abruzzi.

117
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:28.195
Why do you want to see Burrows so bad. anyhow?

118
00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.435
Because he's my brother.

119
00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.471
- They denied the motion.
- Do it again.

120
00:10:55.560 --> 00:11:00.714
I can't. May 11th. That's the date. man.
That's the date they. uh. you know...

121
00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.394
- execute me.
- I know.

122
00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.510
- I didn't kill that man. Michael.
- The evidence says you did.

123
00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.797
I don't care what the evidence says.
I didn't kill him.

124
00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.075
Swear to me.

125
00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.469
I swear to you. Michael.

126
00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.917
But how did they get it wrong. then?
The courts. the appeals...

127
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.468
Don't know. Don't know.

128
00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:36.678
All I keep thinking. looking back on it.
is I was set up.

129
00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:41.197
And whoever it was that set me up wants me
in the ground as quickly as possible.

130
00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:48.037
- What's another word for 'love'?
- What's the context?

131
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:53.433
The 'l love you so much I ain't never
knockin' over a liquor store again' context.

132
00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.795
- Except. you know. classy.
- Mm.

133
00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.633
- I'm proposing to my girl. if you gotta know.
- In a letter?

134
00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:02.234
- You got a better way?
- Face to face is good.

135
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:08.031
This ain't exactly the romantic spot. I'm
gonna have her get on the Staten lsland Ferry.

136
00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.874
then once she can see the Empire
State Building. she opens the letter...

137
00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:16.112
It's like almost being there.
Except for the fact that I won't be there.

138
00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.952
Try 'passion'.

139
00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:21.112
'Passion'.'Passion'. That's dope.

140
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.595
How do you spell that? Is it P-A-S-H...?

141
00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.636
No H?

142
00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.598
- LJ. hold up.
- Hold up?

143
00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:42.959
- I don't think I can go through with this.
- Everything's gonna be fine. Trust me.

144
00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:57.272
We understand each other. then?
Friday. Not Saturday. not Sunday. Friday.

145
00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:00.750
- Totally understood.
- I don't want 100s. fives or ones.

146
00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.673
I know. I know. Tens and 20s only.

147
00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.075
It's on.

148
00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.151
Police!

149
00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.198
Abruzzi. I need you to hire me at Pl.

150
00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.309
- Beat it.
- Maybe you oughta hear what I gotta say.

151
00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:59.595
You got nothing I need.

152
00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.035
- Wouldn't be too sure of that.
- My mistake.

153
00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:08.918
Just what I need. A duck.

154
00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:15.199
Pl. Abruzzi. You might find
I can be of more assistance than you think.

155
00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:21.634
Mull it over.
Come find me when you're ready to talk.

156
00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.230
All right. guys. Pick it up.
I wanna get home tonight.

157
00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:33.311
Maggio?

158
00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.194
- Yeah. So?
- That son of a bitch fingered Abruzzi.

159
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.191
That's Fibonacci?

160
00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.674
- I thought that punk was gone forever.
- Evidently somebody found him.

161
00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:54.788
- Is somebody messin' with us?
- This you're not gonna believe.

162
00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.394
What is it?

163
00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.235
Tattoo looks fresh.
Hold that.

164
00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.479
I guess being a diabetic.
you don't mind needles.

165
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.519
- I'm Michael. by the way.
- Scofield. I read your report.

166
00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.637
- And you are?
- Dr Tancredi will do.

167
00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.314
'Tancredi' like the governor?

168
00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.270
You're not related. are you?

169
00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:28.792
Hm. Wouldn't think you'd find the daughter
of Frontier Justice Frank working in a prison.

170
00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:32.589
- As a doctor. no less.
- I believe in being part of the solution.

171
00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.353
- not the problem.
- Hm.

172
00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.910
'Be the change you want to see in the world.'

173
00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.908
What?

174
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.470
- Nothing. That was just my senior quote.
- That was you?

175
00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.154
This whole time I was thinking it was Gandhi.

176
00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:56.839
You're very funny. Sit tight. Put direct
pressure on that. I'll be back in a sec.

177
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.676
So. how do we play this?
You hook me up with a few weeks' supply?

178
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.274
Nice try. No hypos on the floor.

179
00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:18.113
I'm the farthest thing from a junkie.
Trust me.

180
00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.954
I got news for you.'Trust me'
means absolutely zero inside these walls.

181
00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.635
The only way you're getting that insulin
is if I'm administering it.

182
00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.280
Guess we'll be seeing
a lot of each other. then.

183
00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.555
I guess so.

184
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:45.629
We're all clear on the Burrows execution.
except for one thing.

185
00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.870
Bishop McMorrow is not in the fold.

186
00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:55.713
He's got a lot of influence with the governor.
They went to prep school together apparently.

187
00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.950
Look. the closer it gets.

188
00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:04.115
the more I'm worried that the bottom
is gonna fall out of this whole thing.

189
00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:09.752
Well. maybe it's time you arranged a visit
with the good bishop. then.

190
00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.879
Look. in one month. it'll all be over.

191
00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:18.112
'The Son of Man must be delivered
into the hands of sinful men

192
00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.909
and be crucified.
and the third day rise again.'

193
00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.390
'And they remembered his words.'
And so should you.

194
00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.870
Good day. gentlemen.
May God be with you.

195
00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:41.075
Michael?

196
00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.754
Let's go. Come on. keep moving.

197
00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:50.795
- Why?
- I'm getting you out of here.

198
00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.792
Burrows! Roll it up. Happy hour's over.

199
00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:58.590
- It's impossible.
- Not if you designed the place it isn't.

200
00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.590
Too formal.

201
00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.918
Too greeting-card.

202
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.798
We gotta make a decision
sooner or later. you know.

203
00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:17.668
- We have time.
- We don't. actually.

204
00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.116
At some point
we gotta pull the trigger on this thing.

205
00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:27.389
I don't wanna rush this. We're only
gonna do it once. We have to get it right.

206
00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:34.473
- Honey. can I ask you something?
- Of course.

207
00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.711
- Are you putting this off?
- What do you mean?

208
00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:41.475
- I mean. are you having second thoughts?
- No.

209
00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:44.074
Honey. no. I'm not.

210
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.439
I just can't help thinking this is about...

211
00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.875
It's not.

212
00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:53.839
I love you. And I wanna be your wife.

213
00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:01.116
- 'Passion'? What were you thinking?
- Hey. you went for it.

214
00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.351
She probably thinks
I went sissy up in here.'Passion'.

215
00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.034
Got more than one syllable.
too much talking.

216
00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.509
That's me from now on. One-Syllable Sucre.

217
00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:13.275
'Yes'. 'no'. 'love'. 'hate'...'love'.

218
00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.590
- Give it time.
- Are you kidding?

219
00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:22.392
I proposed to her. That doesn't take time.
'S�' or 'no'. One syllable. man.

220
00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:26.153
She's supposed to come
for a conjugal on Tuesday.

221
00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.073
She always calls me beforehand
to let me know she's coming.

222
00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:32.152
This time. man. I ain't heard a peep.

223
00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.196
You spooked her.

224
00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:39.353
Scofield. Get it together.
Pope wants to see you.

225
00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:46.115
No good. fish.
No one gets an audience with the Pope.

226
00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.510
Not unless he's real interested
in what you got going on.

227
00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:55.229
Top of your class at Loyola.
Magna cum laude. in fact.

228
00:19:55.320 --> 00:20:00.872
I can't help wondering what someone with
your credentials is doing in a place like this.

229
00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.633
Took a wrong turn a few months back. I guess.

230
00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:08.316
You make it sound like a traffic infraction.
like going the wrong way up a one-way street.

231
00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:11.710
Everyone turns up one sooner or later.

232
00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.434
The reason I called you here.

233
00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:22.038
I noticed in your l-file. under 'Occupation'.
you put down 'unemployed'.

234
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.793
That's not true. now. is it?

235
00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:30.553
I know you're a structural engineer. Scofield.

236
00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:35.200
Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal

237
00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:38.670
as a monument to his undying love for his wife.

238
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:41.513
My wife is quite fond of the story.

239
00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.398
It appeals to the romantic in her.

240
00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:51.072
Being married to someone in corrections.
terrible job. Wouldn't wish it on anyone.

241
00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:55.472
And yet. in 39 years.
my wife has never complained.

242
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.597
And the worst part of it is.
I've never thanked her.

243
00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:06.430
So. because I couldn't say it.
I thought. you know. I could build it.

244
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:09.717
Come June. it's our 40th anniversary.

245
00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.952
But here. look...

246
00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.031
You see. the problem is.

247
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:19.636
I build any more. it's all gonna
come down like a house of cards.

248
00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:22.473
That's where I was hoping
you could be of assistance.

249
00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:26.314
And for the favour. I can offer you
three days of work a week in here.

250
00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.994
and it'll keep you off the yard.

251
00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:37.435
I can't do it.

252
00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:42.831
Son. it's better for me to owe you one in here
than it is for you to owe me one.

253
00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.990
I can promise you that.

254
00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.275
I'll take my chances.

255
00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.915
Then we're through here.

256
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.069
Guard!

257
00:21:55.760 --> 00:22:00.151
Two pounds of pot?
What were you trying to do. set a record?

258
00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:04.028
It's not funny. LJ.
You could be going to jail.

259
00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.192
It's pretty obvious to me
you need some guidance.

260
00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:11.077
Hey.

261
00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:13.151
Thanks.

262
00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:17.272
- From who? Old Daddy Warbucks?
- He's a good man.

263
00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.430
We got nothing in common.

264
00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:27.154
Where's this coming from. LJ? Last semester
you were getting almost all As. and now...

265
00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:30.912
- It's your father. isn't it?
- I don't have a father.

266
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.039
It wasn't an immaculate conception. honey.
Trust me.

267
00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:39.113
Maybe it's time you went and saw him.

268
00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:41.074
Mom.

269
00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:43.515
Mom! Don't.

270
00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:46.910
I'm about as excited by that as you are.
but something's gotta give.

271
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:53.075
You have got too much potential
to be screwing up your life like this.

272
00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:57.949
What if they'd sent you
to Taylorville or Marion and not here?

273
00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:02.636
I think I'd be doing the same thing I'm doing
in here - eating Jell-O. drinking Kool-Aid.

274
00:23:02.720 --> 00:23:07.840
I know what you're doing. It's not the luck
of the draw that you're in here with Lincoln.

275
00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:10.150
You forget I know you. Both ofyou.

276
00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:13.710
You two have the most dysfunctional
idea of love I've ever seen.

277
00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:15.950
He beats you up to keep you off the street.

278
00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:18.713
so you get yourself
tossed into Fox River with him?

279
00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:21.189
To what? Save him?

280
00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:26.232
I deserve to know.
I loved him as much as you did.

281
00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:28.675
Past tense for you. maybe. Not me.

282
00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:32.632
I gave him a shot
when I got back from college. I did.

283
00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.157
Even with all the stuff going on. I did all
I could to make it work. and he threw it away.

284
00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:40.994
You ever think maybe he was hurt
that you left in the first place?

285
00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:44.834
Don't do this. Whatever it is you're doing.
there's a better way.

286
00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:47.354
- I'm appealing your case.
- I told you not to.

287
00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:50.159
I got in touch with the diocese about Linc.
The bishop...

288
00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:53.516
That won't stop it. It'll only delay it.

289
00:23:56.960 --> 00:24:02.034
You wanna do something?
You find out who's trying to bury him.

290
00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:06.476
Nobody's trying to bury him.
The evidence was there.

291
00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:08.278
The evidence was cooked.

292
00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.360
Visiting hours are now over.

293
00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:19.911
Take care of yourself.

294
00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:26.070
Someone wants him dead. Veronica.
Something more is going on here.

295
00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:29.072
This is desperation. Michael.
You're in denial.

296
00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:31.958
Maybe. But I can't watch him die.

297
00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:34.395
I won't do that.

298
00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:02.989
Gentlemen.

299
00:25:03.080 --> 00:25:06.550
What is it about the Burrows situation
that I can help you with?

300
00:25:06.640 --> 00:25:10.349
It's our understanding that you have
great influence with the governor.

301
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:14.319
I wouldn't say it's great. or influence.
We're friends.

302
00:25:14.400 --> 00:25:17.631
It's also our understanding
that you oppose the death penalty.

303
00:25:17.720 --> 00:25:20.359
- I'm a man of God. How could I not?
- In this case.

304
00:25:20.440 --> 00:25:24.433
we're hoping you'll suspend that position.
at least temporarily.

305
00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:29.594
If the inmate appeals to me for intervention.
how can I turn my back on him?

306
00:25:29.680 --> 00:25:32.478
You have a habit of answering a question
with a question.

307
00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:37.839
And you have a way of asking questions
that beg more questions.

308
00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:43.432
- Are you saying you won't do it?
- I'm not a man to equivocate.

309
00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:50.869
- You're. what. 62 now. Your Excellency?
- That's right.

310
00:25:50.960 --> 00:25:54.157
So you should be well versed
in how the tax system works.

311
00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:58.279
Taking personal capital gains
under the church's tax shelter.

312
00:25:58.360 --> 00:26:01.352
that would be fraud.
wouldn't it. Your Excellency?

313
00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:05.672
I will not be cowed into forsaking my beliefs.

314
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:07.671
Not by you. or anyone else.

315
00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:10.517
Admirable.

316
00:26:10.600 --> 00:26:13.034
Good day. Excellency.

317
00:26:13.120 --> 00:26:19.150
Mr Kellerman. what is it about this case
that the Secret Service is so interested in?

318
00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:23.395
The man killed the Vice-President's brother.

319
00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:31.430
- What did you say?
- You heard me.

320
00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:34.956
Someone found Fibonacci.
I'm looking at the photos right now.

321
00:26:35.040 --> 00:26:39.636
Son of a bitch has got a beard. sunglasses.
Witness protection ifl ever saw it.

322
00:26:39.720 --> 00:26:41.119
Who was this someone?

323
00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:45.990
Don't know. There's no return address
on the envelope. Just...

324
00:26:46.080 --> 00:26:48.640
this folded-up bird. made of paper.

325
00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:53.479
- Like origami?
- Yeah. like that.

326
00:26:53.560 --> 00:26:55.755
Like origami.

327
00:27:28.240 --> 00:27:31.277
- You're Charles Westmoreland. right?
- Do I know you?

328
00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:34.750
- I knew your wife. before she passed.
- You knew Marla?

329
00:27:34.840 --> 00:27:38.037
- You mean Ann?
- How'd you know her?

330
00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:40.873
- We taught together in Boston.
- East Farmington.

331
00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:43.349
You mean West Wilmington?

332
00:27:43.440 --> 00:27:45.908
No more tests. I promise.

333
00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:50.552
Seems you know everything about me.
Who are you?

334
00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:53.996
Michael Scofield.
How'd you get it in here?

335
00:27:54.080 --> 00:27:56.150
First off. she's not an it.

336
00:27:56.240 --> 00:27:59.676
She's Marilyn.
and she's grandfathered back from the days

337
00:27:59.760 --> 00:28:03.355
when prisoners were allowed
a creature comfort or two.

338
00:28:03.440 --> 00:28:05.635
Heard you were DB Cooper.

339
00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:12.158
Every new fish that comes in. first thing they
hear is Charles Westmoreland's DB Cooper.

340
00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:14.708
I'll tell you like I tell them.

341
00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:20.396
You want the Cooper story?
I can't give it to you. cos I'm not him.

342
00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:24.393
That's too bad. I sort of wish it was true.
The man's a legend.

343
00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:27.597
Nowhere near as much
as I wish it were true. friend.

344
00:28:27.680 --> 00:28:31.958
I'd have a million five
waiting for me on the outside.

345
00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:36.955
I'd put some grass under 'em if I were you.

346
00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:40.157
This thing'd go a whole lot easier
if you'd just hire me.

347
00:28:40.240 --> 00:28:42.549
What is this all about?

348
00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:45.552
Say you were able to get outside those walls.

349
00:28:45.640 --> 00:28:48.438
Are there people in place
to make you disappear forever?

350
00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:51.273
- What do you care?
- I'm just curious.

351
00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:55.558
- Where's Fibonacci?
- That's not the way it works.

352
00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:02.796
They come at me. John. I'm coming after you.

353
00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:05.235
I doubt it.

354
00:29:30.640 --> 00:29:32.517
All right.

355
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.636
Get on the ground.

356
00:29:40.720 --> 00:29:45.157
I totally misjudged you. Scofield.
I didn't think you were the agitating type.

357
00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:47.993
Behaviour like that
will not be tolerated in my prison.

358
00:29:48.080 --> 00:29:51.231
90 days in the SHU oughta be
enough time to convince you of that.

359
00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:53.709
- 90 days?
- That's right.

360
00:30:00.840 --> 00:30:04.230
- Something you wanna say?
- It's just...

361
00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:08.630
- I'm not of much value to you in the SHU.
- Value?

362
00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:12.554
The Taj. It'd be a shame for the eighth wonder
of the modern world to collapse

363
00:30:12.640 --> 00:30:14.870
because the stress isn't properly propagated.

364
00:30:14.960 --> 00:30:17.872
- Properly propagated?
- Properly propagated.

365
00:30:17.960 --> 00:30:19.791
The joints are overloaded.

366
00:30:19.880 --> 00:30:24.829
They won't provide anywhere near the sheer
strength the completed structure will need.

367
00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:28.151
- How much work are we talking?
- You want it by when. June?

368
00:30:28.240 --> 00:30:30.913
- Yes.
- Then we'd better get started.

369
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:32.752
wouldn't you say?

370
00:30:58.040 --> 00:31:00.031
Who's there?

371
00:31:16.720 --> 00:31:21.396
Bishop McMorrow was killed last night.
Someone shot him while he was sleeping.

372
00:31:21.480 --> 00:31:24.438
- I thought you'd wanna know.
- Thanks.

373
00:31:31.640 --> 00:31:34.234
Michael was right.

374
00:32:01.360 --> 00:32:03.476
Sink! You got a visitor.

375
00:32:15.400 --> 00:32:16.992
He was arrested.

376
00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:21.631
- For what?
- Possession of marijuana.

377
00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:28.477
I figured he could use
some fatherly advice before it's...

378
00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:30.391
- Gone forever?
- I didn't mean that.

379
00:32:30.480 --> 00:32:33.153
I know you didn't. Thanks. Lisa.

380
00:32:34.520 --> 00:32:36.511
So...

381
00:32:40.560 --> 00:32:43.358
Dope. huh? Using or dealing?

382
00:32:44.880 --> 00:32:47.394
- What's the difference?
- Then what?

383
00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:51.359
You think it gives you
some kind of street cred?

384
00:32:51.440 --> 00:32:54.796
You've got a piece of the good life.
Take advantage.

385
00:32:54.880 --> 00:32:57.792
Look. I get it. The whole thing.

386
00:32:57.880 --> 00:33:03.034
She drags me in here. you give me
a big speech. I walk away a changed man.

387
00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:07.159
Straight As. Harvard.
grow up and be a dentist.

388
00:33:07.240 --> 00:33:09.834
It's better than being here.

389
00:33:10.960 --> 00:33:13.952
You gotta realise who gets punished
when you do what you do.

390
00:33:14.040 --> 00:33:17.316
You think it's me. It's you.
I did the same thing.

391
00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:22.520
Punished the old man cos he was gone.
Look where it got me.

392
00:33:23.760 --> 00:33:28.959
I'm not asking you to love me.
I already screwed up that chance long ago.

393
00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:35.229
I'm asking you to love yourself.
You can still put the brakes on this thing.

394
00:33:35.320 --> 00:33:39.393
- So that's what fatherly advice is like.
- Where are you going?

395
00:33:40.760 --> 00:33:44.435
- I got homework.
- They're putting me to death. LJ.

396
00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:48.589
In a month's time. I'll be dead.
You get that?

397
00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:52.829
You're already dead to me.

398
00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:04.751
Co�o.

399
00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:17.514
Yes.

400
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.594
What. you mean 'yes. yes'?

401
00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:23.230
- Yes! Yes!
- Yeah!

402
00:34:25.600 --> 00:34:27.397
- Just one thing.
- Of course.

403
00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:30.119
- My mom wants us to wait till you get out.
- Of course.

404
00:34:30.200 --> 00:34:33.590
And we have to get married in a church.
A Catholic church.

405
00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:37.673
Wouldn't want to mess
with the Catholic roots. would we?

406
00:34:42.240 --> 00:34:44.834
- You went to Loyola.
- You've been checking up on me.

407
00:34:44.920 --> 00:34:48.708
I like to get to know my patients.
I went to Northwestern.

408
00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:50.392
Maybe we met before.

409
00:34:50.480 --> 00:34:53.313
- Drunk. out at a bar somewhere.
- I would have remembered.

410
00:34:53.400 --> 00:34:55.550
- That a compliment?
- No.

411
00:34:56.560 --> 00:34:58.596
Hm.

412
00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:02.070
- What?
- Your blood glucose is 50mg per decilitre.

413
00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:04.230
- So?
- It's hypoglycaemic.

414
00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:07.073
Your body is reacting
like you're not a diabetic.

415
00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:12.109
- You sure it's type 1 diabetes you've got?
- Ever since I was a kid.

416
00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:15.875
- Any tingling. cold sweats?
- 

417
00:35:18.560 --> 00:35:19.993
Infirmary.

418
00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:22.310
Yes.

419
00:35:22.400 --> 00:35:24.391
Yeah. he did.

420
00:35:25.200 --> 00:35:27.668
No. I did one a week ago.

421
00:35:28.480 --> 00:35:30.471
OK.

422
00:35:30.560 --> 00:35:34.758
Great. Well. I'll call him after lunch. then.
Thanks. I'm with a patient. OK.

423
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:37.274
I'd like to run some tests next time you're in.

424
00:35:37.360 --> 00:35:40.272
I don't want to administer insulin
to a man who doesn't need it.

425
00:35:40.360 --> 00:35:42.316
Yeah. Sure.

426
00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:44.197
OK.

427
00:35:50.360 --> 00:35:54.353
- How'd you get here. by the way?
- Oh. you know.

428
00:35:54.440 --> 00:35:56.715
I don't. That's why I asked.

429
00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:59.872
- You know... Hector.
- What?!

430
00:35:59.960 --> 00:36:06.274
I didn't have any money for the bus.
so he offered me a ride. He was really sweet.

431
00:36:06.360 --> 00:36:10.638
- Honey. he's just a friend.
- No. he's not. I know Hector. I know men.

432
00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:15.919
Men and women can't be friends. A guy
doesn't drive a girl 500 miles to be friends.

433
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:19.072
Casanova! Wrap it up.

434
00:36:19.160 --> 00:36:24.029
Hey. You got nothing to worry about. OK?
It's you I'm marrying.

435
00:36:24.120 --> 00:36:26.714
It's not you I'm worried about.

436
00:36:28.360 --> 00:36:30.555
Sixteen more months.

437
00:36:38.680 --> 00:36:40.671
I love you.

438
00:36:50.920 --> 00:36:52.911
Be easy. son. all right?

439
00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:02.150
Sucre tells me you're the local pharmacy.

440
00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:06.830
- What do you need. man?
- PUGNAc.

441
00:37:06.920 --> 00:37:10.230
- I only speak English. white boy.
- It's an insulin blocker.

442
00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:12.880
Standard variety.
You can get it at any pharmacy.

443
00:37:12.960 --> 00:37:15.599
- You can get that at Medical. then.
- I can't.

444
00:37:15.680 --> 00:37:20.196
- Why not?
- Because they're giving me insulin shots.

445
00:37:21.200 --> 00:37:25.830
- You're one mixed-up cracker.
- Can you get it for me or not?

446
00:37:25.920 --> 00:37:29.037
Only if you tell me
why you keep going back to Medical

447
00:37:29.120 --> 00:37:33.033
- to get an insulin shot you don't need.
- I like the ambience.

448
00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:35.509
- A-ha.
- Are we in business?

449
00:37:50.600 --> 00:37:55.628
Scofield! I don't know what you did. but
Abruzzi wanted me to give you this Pl card.

450
00:37:55.720 --> 00:38:00.794
Congratulations.
You just joined the ranks of the employed.

451
00:38:14.600 --> 00:38:17.876
Kudos. fish. You got spine.

452
00:38:23.720 --> 00:38:26.314
All right. cons! Break it down.

453
00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:30.071
Move. you guys.

454
00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:44.077
Saw Veronica came by yesterday.
Still engaged to that guy?

455
00:38:44.160 --> 00:38:46.549
- Yup.
- It could have been me.

456
00:38:46.640 --> 00:38:49.313
If you hadn't self-destructed.

457
00:38:49.400 --> 00:38:54.997
You think I meant to knock up Lisa Rix?
I was just being stupid. Hurt.

458
00:38:56.000 --> 00:39:00.039
- Shouldn't have pushed her away. though.
- You pushed everyone away.

459
00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:04.477
I'm an anchor.
All I'll do is drag 'em down with me.

460
00:39:08.560 --> 00:39:11.518
- Why'd you hire him?
- Keep your friends close.

461
00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:13.909
and your enemies closer.

462
00:39:18.640 --> 00:39:22.474
- Did you mean what you said earlier?
- I'm not here on vacation. Trust me.

463
00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:29.192
Getting outside these walls is just
the beginning. You're gonna need money.

464
00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.672
I'll have it.

465
00:39:32.760 --> 00:39:36.719
And people on the outside.
People that can help you disappear.

466
00:39:36.800 --> 00:39:38.995
I've already got 'em.

467
00:39:39.080 --> 00:39:41.674
They just don't know it yet.

468
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:50.433
Look. whatever you've got going on.
fill me in. cos I'm in the dark here.

469
00:39:50.520 --> 00:39:55.275
Chaparral Associates got the contract
to retrofit this place in '99 - $4 million.

470
00:39:55.360 --> 00:40:00.832
Head partner couldn't crack it. so he
subcontracted out to a former associate.

471
00:40:00.920 --> 00:40:04.595
That guy was one of the partners in my firm.

472
00:40:05.880 --> 00:40:11.750
We ghost-wrote the whole plan - crossed
the t's. dotted the i's. grouted the tiles.

473
00:40:19.440 --> 00:40:23.115
- You've seen the blueprints.
- Better than that.

474
00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:24.872
I've got 'em on me.

475
00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:30.915
Are you kidding me?

476
00:40:33.320 --> 00:40:37.598
- Am I supposed to see something here?
- Look closer.

477
00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:43.873
Visiontext Subtitles: Paul Murray

478
00:41:49.200 --> 00:41:51.031
ENGLISH SDH

